From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:09:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] airconv: 64-bit groupshared atomics through a threadgroup
 lock array.

Shader Model 6.6's 64-bit atomics on groupshared memory are LLVM atomicrmw/cmpxchg of i64 on addrspace(3), with no
dx.op; Metal has no threadgroup ulong atomics and its compiler service crashed on them, so they were refused. They
now run under a lock array (spec 3.8): 256 u32 locks (1 KiB) in threadgroup memory, or the largest power of two that
fits beside the shader's own groupshared memory in 32768 bytes (refused by name when not even one fits). Thread i
zeroes slots i, i + group, ... at the body's start, then one threadgroup barrier; each atomic takes lock
(byte offset >> 3) & (N - 1) through UnderLock with threadgroup fences at threadgroup scope, reads and writes the qword
with plain loads and stores, and a compare-exchange stores only on a match. A compute shader with such an atomic
gets the flattened thread index even when no dx.op reads it. DXC emits no other atomicrmw; any other is refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
